{"title":"2007 IMO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Resources\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Resources</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(<i>Kevin Buzzard and Edward Crane, United Kingdom</i>)\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> be positive integers.  Show that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/0/c60ffe33c6a761319599d4dd52e41de142e8da64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4ab-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/9/5c96ed932b34322b755fd71e93a4476ca2a541e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4a^2-1)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"19\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5abd2c942ae299fd26e18d0ca5d390a7ca4a8c34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=b$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><b>Lemma.</b> If there is a counterexample for some value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, then there is a counterexample <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8da0aef2d19017da7471378386d61620f288f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> for this value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43bbd1a828df9121a4ae64a2638aad54f7520f43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&lt;a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><i>Proof.</i>  Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/2/b02906935e5e9e069c5018bb94a1b89e353af51a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b &gt;a$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" />.  Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/6/7469a6b1343dd3fd76c6fa6311c01372a9b663be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4ab -1 \\equiv -1 \\pmod{4a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"185\" height=\"18\" />, but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/c/bec870018d4ecd8af16d036ca7162c3f398d5017.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4a^2-1)^2 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{4a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"192\" height=\"19\" />.  It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/c/ffc6f567853e4a72b2a3e812a1a4eff3cc438050.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4a^2-1)^2/(4ab-1) \\equiv -1 \\pmod{4a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"287\" height=\"19\" />.  Since\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/2/9a269c019f5c52c28756b17a23a9f858431ae4f5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[0&lt;(4a^2-1)^2/(4ab-1) &lt; (4a^2-1)^2/(4a^2-1) = 4a^2-1,\\]\" width=\"462\" height=\"19\" />\nit follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/b/47b51127d09a290ae1e7cc0d565a72a8427f721f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4a^2-1)^2/(4ab-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"158\" height=\"19\" /> can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/1/191fff90f612aa40dc83945f12d441173d1d16ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4ab&#39;-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/c/99c9cf8bdd85a40e14f28cc843852201db0646ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;b&#39;&lt;a$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"79\" height=\"14\" />.  Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/9/1c94c6c4b9cd9c294b137d051b8d9aa34503100a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b&#39;)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"18\" /> is a counterexample for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/6/1160cc9d11c15c37fbd81622e8321f19c3b718ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&#39;&lt;a$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Now, suppose a counterexample exists.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8da0aef2d19017da7471378386d61620f288f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> be a counterexample for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is minimal and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43bbd1a828df9121a4ae64a2638aad54f7520f43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&lt;a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />.  We note that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/1/42163e82c6450d732b5980447b41e3cc723f11e9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\gcd(4ab-1,2a-1) \\mid 4ab-1 - 2b(2a-1) = 2b-1,\\]\" width=\"409\" height=\"18\" />\nand\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/3/593e358b5cbd98449bdd44e597f56df26fa2f7f1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\gcd(4ab-1,2a+1) \\mid 2b(2a+1) - (4ab-1) = 2b+1 .\\]\" width=\"423\" height=\"18\" />\nNow,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/8/2b82ec450ac3d3b279bc1505e1ab147ebf435367.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 4ab-1 &amp;\\mid (4a^2-1)^2 = (2a-1)^2(2a+1)^2 \\\\ &amp;\\mid \\gcd(4ab-1,2a-1)^2 \\cdot \\gcd(4ab-1,2a+1)^2 \\\\ &amp;\\mid (2b-1)^2(2b+1)^2 = (4b^2-1)^2 . \\end{align*}\" width=\"413\" height=\"75\" />\nThus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/3/963a27195c32f1708f62bb2c0e82add2d45486dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(b,a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> is a counterexample.  But <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43bbd1a828df9121a4ae64a2638aad54f7520f43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&lt;a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />, which contradicts the minimality of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />.  Therefore no counterexample exists.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><br />\n(<i>Sean Yu, US</i>)\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/f/4ff72c5b8531397d0da96a8f0e98ba9e5ec0238c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4a^2-1)^2 = (4a^2-4ab + 4ab-1)^2 \\equiv (4a)^2(a-b)^2 \\pmod {4ab-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"528\" height=\"21\" />, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/6/3369da3278dc387e695fa4e06fc7016d3c3b1413.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$gcd((4a)^2, 4ab -1 ) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"182\" height=\"21\" />,  we only need to show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/f/0cf11be689fd8441f41b6e0a323490ba74f14fa0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4ab -1 \\mid (a-b)^2 \\Rightarrow a=b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"206\" height=\"21\" />. We will use the Vieta Jumping technique to solve it. \n</p><p>Suppose there exist  counterexamples, which means the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/4/644cbe2f1d95132dc034c4021909a3299874292c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = \\{(x, y): \\mbox {x and y are positive integers}, x \\ne y, 4xy-1 \\mid (x-y)^2\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"519\" height=\"21\" /> is not empty. Then there exists a pair <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/4/2140ef50756ef8adc17c880f53e62107bdacb036.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b)\\in S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"20\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> has the minimum sum among all pairs in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />. Without loss of generality, we assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/d/25d8ed1fc54739081e1cc984b300a5b1bd0a984f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &gt; b$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/0/750398fd1766f547f1eaa7597531a9540da6fccb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=\\frac{(a-b)^2}{4ab-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"101\" height=\"42\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is a positive integer and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/f/66f112f3b989bcebedd01a7a912a149899e1ab3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2-(2+4k)ba + b^2+k = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"226\" height=\"21\" />. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is a root for the quadratic equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/e/bfeb5515e2cff70f3bd4f28f1ab40e225d90f811.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2-(2+4k)bx + b^2+k = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"228\" height=\"21\" />. Using the Vieta Lemma, we know the equation has another root <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/a/35abb27e5f4327aaad779480f8e984a584694cdf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&#39; = \\frac{b^2 + k}{a} &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"125\" height=\"41\" /> and from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/0/210b9f51527851a95d3677633bf5ac5c3859ebb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&#39; = (2+4k)b -a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"145\" height=\"20\" /> we know it is an integer. Note that since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/2/f1279ffb2af6d892d6fa08a258ad77784f33d6ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4ab -1 \\mid(a-b)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"136\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/2/082852571ecc48ed136ba13dcffa8f6e40064bbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/e/d3e67e890c7aca5504ce9f100e886d5eefb48bf2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4ab -1 \\le (a-b)^2 \\le a^2-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"218\" height=\"21\" />, which implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/9/ef96b5668869a028ae176c83dcc1440fee89ea90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b\\le a/4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"62\" height=\"20\" />. Also  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/4/0a4079b8bb201a20e557f31ad073602db8425798.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=\\frac{(a-b)^2}{4ab-1} \\le \\frac{a^2}{3ab} \\le a/3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"208\" height=\"42\" />, thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/8/828cf94734f7a99dcda2ee7f5de5534bd845c8b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&#39; = \\frac{b^2 + k}{a} \\le \\frac{(a/4)^2 + a/3}{a} = a/16 + 1/3 &lt; a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"364\" height=\"41\" />, and we get another pair <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/e/f4e62fe1ce3a13953358df018e720a9536bebaa3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a&#39;, b)\\in S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"81\" height=\"20\" />, but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/e/a4edc59620413ad92606ea2885fb0a8d2a220a6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&#39; + b &lt; a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"110\" height=\"17\" />, which contradicts the assumption that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> has the minimum sum.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/2/7828ca8f949024e9771acdc0d0747d61ced53551.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\hfill\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/3/613a4ef57e2b0c0fb2d6490e8da4fbd3e4229c5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4a^2-1)^2=(2a-1)^2(2a+1)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"248\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>and\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/5/c95240a6029548babff13080425bcd1d36df636b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gcd(2a-1,2a+1)=1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"190\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Hence,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/6/82695d988e1ac1da176071865edcf24e004cc3bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4ab-1 \\mid (2a-1)(2a+1)=4a^2-1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"290\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/4/c349fa881d5b48aa600497864a2f845ddb086623.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b\\ge1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/b/6cb157d473589beab14fe3d30f69676e02434f23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4ab-1 \\ge 4a-1 &gt; 2a+1 &gt; 2a-1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"287\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>it follows that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/3/a13f1143e034bf5afa572c7cd0c262af3683558d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4ab-1=4a^2-1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"146\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Thus,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/3/bb32bb2ed94d0f3200b90c5d4fbadb13ea8fb0f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=b.$\" width=\"45\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>(Hoang Bach - Vietnam)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO\" title=\"2007 IMO\">2007 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2007 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2007 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2007 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2007 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2007 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2007 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2007 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2007 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<ul><li>&lt;url&gt;viewtopic.php?p=894656#p894656 Discussion on AoPS/MathLinks&lt;/url&gt;</li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016220013\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.034 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.054 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 353/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 11741/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    9.446      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    9.446      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6769:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261016220013 and revision id 276035. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}